    "difficultyReason": "There is no diagram, so the student must turn the x-values 1 and 3 into y-limits 1 and 9, rewrite y=x^2 as x=√y, and integrate with respect to y. That is one representation change plus limit conversion, then a routine integral with a simple root. It is a little more than a direct area-by-y integral, but easier than p20-q8, which needs a shifted cube-root inverse and a check on which side of the axis the region lies.",
